# Phase progress tracking

## Before starting implementation work

1. Read [`docs/PROGRESS.md`](docs/PROGRESS.md) (status board) and the matching phase in [`docs/SRS.md`](docs/SRS.md).
2. Only work on the **Active phase**. Do not start later-phase items unless the user explicitly overrides.
3. Set the item you are about to do to `[~]`, update **Current focus** (`Active item`, `Last updated`, `Last note`).

## While / after finishing a chunk of work

1. Mark finished checklist items `[x]`. Leave unrelated items untouched.
2. If blocked, mark `[!]` and note why under **Current focus** → `Last note`; optionally add `docs/notes/blocker-….md`.
3. When every item under a phase (including its quality gate) is `[x]`, mark that phase overview line `[x]` and move **Active phase** to the next number.
4. Append one row to **Session log** (date, phase, short change summary).
5. Ending a long session → also write `docs/handoffs/YYYYMMDD-….md` (see that folder's README).
6. Do **not** rewrite SRS acceptance lists as a substitute for `PROGRESS.md` — SRS stays the spec; PROGRESS stays the status.

## Doc map

See `docs/README.md` and root `AGENTS.md` for architecture / decisions / design / notes / prompts.

## Checkbox markers

- `[ ]` not started · `[~]` in progress · `[x]` done · `[!]` blocked
